## Architecture Overview (DDD)

This project follows Domain-Driven Design (DDD) layered architecture principles:

```
├── cmd/
│   └── server/          # Application entrypoint & composition root (main.go)
├── internal/
│   ├── domain/          # Core business entities, value objects, domain events & repository interfaces
│   │   ├── model/       # Aggregate roots and domain models
│   │   ├── repository/  # Repository abstraction interfaces (zero infrastructure dependencies)
│   │   ├── event/       # Domain event structures
│   │   └── valueobject/ # Immutable value objects
│   ├── application/     # Application use cases, services, DTOs & primary ports
│   │   ├── service/     # Use case orchestrators (depends only on domain)
│   │   ├── dto/         # Request/Response data transfer objects
│   │   └── port/        # Inbound and outbound port interfaces
│   ├── infrastructure/  # Concrete adapters (databases, external clients, configuration)
│   │   ├── persistence/ # Concrete repository implementations
│   │   ├── config/      # Environment configuration loading
│   │   └── client/      # External service HTTP/gRPC clients
│   └── interfaces/      # Inbound presentation layer (HTTP handlers, gRPC servers)
│       ├── http/        # REST API handlers, routing, middleware
│       └── grpc/        # gRPC server implementation
└── pkg/                 # Shared utilities (logger, error types)
```

